An undeclared name read in a procedure body (diag.undeclared_variable).
The check is opt-in, so it appears only under the strict profile, once
per name per file even when the name is read twice. A name created by
assignment (nShipped) is not undeclared.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE TallyCrates;
	:PARAMETERS nPerCrate;
	:DECLARE nTotal;
	nTotal := nCrateCount * nPerCrate;
	nShipped := nTotal;
	:IF nCrateCount > 10;
		nTotal := nTotal + 1;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nTotal + nShipped;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE TallyCrates;
	:PARAMETERS nPerCrate;
	:DECLARE nTotal;

	nTotal := nCrateCount * nPerCrate;
	nShipped := nTotal;

	:IF nCrateCount > 10;
		nTotal := nTotal + 1;
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN nTotal + nShipped;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:12-4:23 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'nCrateCount' is not declared
